# Use writes of `c` no more than "a text or a list": it is read under an index and asked for its length. But `c` holds what is read off a field, and the field's own class writes floats into it: the text of the
# file. The two do not meet, and a bare word of use says less: the floats are expected, tested once in front of the loop.
# f1 = go
# RUN: walk f1:Body mechanisms=all
# CHECK: = TypeTest {{*}} testedType=Float64Array
# CHECK: = GetTypedArrayElement
# RUN(ANSWERS): run-in-shell globalThis.sink = () => {};
# ANSWERS: 8 16
